Notes for anyone touching this packaging
========================================

Three things about this source package are not obvious from debian/rules.

The CMake project is not at the top level
-----------------------------------------

telebit-fcitx5/CMakeLists.txt builds the Fcitx 5 addon, the `telebit` command
and the telebit-setup window; the CMakeLists.txt in the root builds only the
conversion engine's own test binary. The addon sources reach back up into the
root for vietnamese.cpp and engine.cpp, so the tree must stay intact — hence
`dh $@ --sourcedirectory=telebit-fcitx5` rather than moving anything.

A consequence: `dh_auto_test` runs the addon's ctest suite (the doctor tests),
not the root conversion-engine suite. Upstream CI runs both.

The tarball is repacked
-----------------------

debian/copyright carries Files-Excluded for dict/, node_modules/, site/ and
.venv/, and debian/watch adds repacksuffix=+ds. dict/ is the interesting one:
it holds two word lists used by scripts/dict-roundtrip/run.sh, a regression
harness that is not part of the build-time tests. dict/vietnamese is derived
from hunspell-vi and is GPL-2 — free, but it would put a second licence into
an otherwise MIT source package to review, for data that is already in the
archive as hunspell-vi and wamerican. Nothing in the build reads it.

If a future version wires that harness into the build, the exclusion has to be
revisited rather than worked around.

environment.d is deliberately disabled
--------------------------------------

Upstream installs /usr/lib/environment.d/60-telebit-fcitx5.conf, which points
GTK_IM_MODULE, QT_IM_MODULE and XMODIFIERS at fcitx5 for the whole graphical
session. That is a reasonable default for a package installed from upstream's
own APT repository, but in Debian that choice belongs to im-config: one engine
package must not select the session's input method framework on behalf of every
other one. debian/rules therefore passes
-DTELEBIT_INSTALL_ENVIRONMENTD=OFF, and users run `im-config -n fcitx5`.

This is worth mentioning in the package description of any derivative that
re-enables it.

Maintainer is the upstream author, not the team
-----------------------------------------------

debian/control names the upstream author. ITP #1147199 states the intent to
maintain this inside the Debian Input Method Team, which is where the other
fcitx5-* engines live, but the team has not adopted the package yet. Naming a
team that has not agreed would speak for them. When they do adopt it, move
Maintainer to the team address and put the author under Uploaders.
